WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.232
"Can NAD+ Boosters Increase
Lifespan and Healthspan?"

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:10.040
The effects of NAD+ boosters
on aged rodents

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:11.840
have been described
in the medical literature

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:16.120
as “profound,” “dramatic”…
“remarkable….”

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:19.720
Treated mice had increased
physical activity, improved vision,

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:23.160
and strengthened bones while
delaying or preventing muscle loss,

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:27.880
hearing loss, cognitive decline,
and ovarian aging.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:31.520
Benefits to nearly every organ
system have been documented,

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:35.720
including improved artery function,
brain function,

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:39.000
heart function,
immune function,

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.600
kidney function, liver function,
and muscle function.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:46.360
For example, a single week of an
NAD+ booster was sufficient

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:50.560
to restore key markers of muscle
health in a 22-month-old mouse

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:53.000
to levels similar to that
of a 6-month-old mouse.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:56.040
That’s roughly the equivalent
of reverting the muscle health

00:00:56.040 --> 00:01:00.320
of a 70-year-old person back
to when they were just 20.

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:03.400
NAD+ boosters can also extend
the lifespans of animals,

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:08.360
presumed to be due to the elevation
of sirtuin activity dependent on NAD+.

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:10.280
This longevity effect
was first demonstrated

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:12.880
more than 20 years
ago in yeast cells.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:16.800
An overexpression of the genes
involved in NAD+ synthesis

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:20.680
extended replicative lifespans
by as much as 60%.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:23.000
In the microscopic
worm C. elegans,

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.960
NAD+-boosting compounds
have been shown

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:27.760
to extend lifespans
by up to 16%.

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:31.600
In mice, one NAD+ booster
was able to extend lifespan

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:33.840
by a more modest 5%,

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:37.240
but this was accomplished even when
supplementation was started late in life,

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:40.400
which is unusual for
longevity treatments.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:45.680
No wonder people are excited about
all manner of NAD+ boosting supplements.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:49.360
The big question is do any of
these healthspan or lifespan effects

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:53.480
translate to benefiting humans?

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:57.160
There are four major NAD+ boosting
supplements on the market these days:

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:59.840
nicotinic acid (NA),
also known as niacin,

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:04.040
nicotinamide (NAM),
also known as niacinamide,

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:06.680
nicotinamide riboside (NR),

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:10.200
and nicotinamide
mononucleotide (NMN).

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:14.680
NAD+ can also be given directly,
as well as its hydrogenated form NADH.

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:18.080
There are also hydrogenated
forms of NMN and NR,

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:21.080
also known as
dihydronicotinamide riboside.

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:24.040
So, there is quite
the alphabet soup:

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:30.320
NA, NAM, NMN, NR, NAD,
NADH, NMNH, and NRH.

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:32.280
The body can also make
NAD+ “from scratch”

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:35.280
from the amino
acid tryptophan.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:36.800
Given the critical
nature of NAD+,

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:40.000
it is perhaps unsurprising that the
body has so many different pathways

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:43.160
utilizing a panoply
of precursors.

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:46.040
Converting tryptophan to
NAD+ requires eight steps,

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:50.920
whereas NA, NAM, and NR can be turned
into NAD+ in only two or three steps.

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:54.440
NMN is a direct
precursor of NAD+,

00:02:54.440 --> 00:03:00.320
but when NMN or NR is taken orally,
it appears to just turn into NA or NAM,

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:02.880
via rapid degradation
in the bloodstream

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:05.080
or active conversion in the liver.

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:07.840
So, why take the more
expensive NMN or NR

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:10.960
if it’s just going to end
up as NA or NAM?

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:15.000
Bought in bulk, NA or NAM
would just cost pennies a day

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:18.560
versus more like a dollar
a day for NR or NMN.

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:22.040
That would add up to hundreds
of dollars a year for NR or NMN

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:28.000
compared to closer to only five bucks
for a whole year’s worth of NA or NAM.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:33.400
But cost aside, what are the risks
and benefits of all these NAD boosters?

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:37.772
That’s exactly what I’ll cover, next.

